  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe premise here is to have a custom element, let's call it `<x-select>`, that customizes the styling of the select. It could be part of a design system for example. In the most simple version of that custom element, the options would be slotted into the select:\n\n```html\n<div id=\"host\">\n  <template shadowrootmode=\"open\">\n    <style>\n      select, ::picker(select) {\n        appearance: base-select;\n      }\n    </style>\n    <select>\n      <slot></slot>\n    </select>\n  </template>\n  <option>slotted: A</option>\n  <option>slotted: B</option>\n  <option>slotted: C</option>\n</div>\n```\n\nIf i try this in Chromium, i do see the options in the dropdown, but you cannot hover or select them.\n\nThere a codepen from @sorvell at https://codepen.io/Steve-Orvell/pen/VYjQYVb?editors=1010 that has the same end result, but involves quite a bit of extra complexity.\n\nCan we avoid the extra complexity needed and get the \"simple\" version above working?",
